"Connects circular category arcs with ribbons whose widths encode weighted pairwise relationships.\n\nUse when: A small weighted relationship matrix needs an overview of dominant connections. Circular arrangement adds value and direction semantics can be explained clearly.\n\nAvoid when: Many categories or ribbons make relationships difficult to follow.\n\nVisual grammar: Arc extent encodes the category’s incident total under a declared convention. Ribbon endpoint widths encode matrix values; asymmetric or directed flows require explicit direction encoding.\n\nBuild: Prepare the weighted category matrix and decide how self-links and direction work. Order categories and ribbons to reduce avoidable intersections. Draw proportional arcs and ribbons with labels beyond the circle and generous label clearance.\n\nCheck: Check matrix orientation and any directed-arrow convention. Verify totals do not double-count symmetric relationships. Confirm ribbon widths match their endpoint quantities.\n\nPitfalls: Ribbon crossings are intrinsic and should never be fixed by changing quantities. Prefer a matrix heatmap by default when the main task is identifying exact category pairs or values.\n\nExample: Show synthetic transfers among six clubs using a directed matrix, outside arc labels, and proportional ribbon endpoints.\n\nAlternatives: Sankey diagram, Heatmap, Alluvial diagram."
